WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.934
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:04.300
Guys, I'm super excited
about this.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.767
The one and only, Dolly Parton,
is my guest tonight!

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:09.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.367
Dolly!

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:14.567
Right now, thousands of people
outside are like,

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:16.601
"Screw the tree lighting.
I want to see Dolly."

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:19.000
Come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:23.467
I'm excited to ask Dolly
about her new Christmas special,

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:25.501
her new album,
and ask her for advice

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:28.167
on building my theme park,
Jimmy Wood.

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:32.968
[ Guitar plays chord ]

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:35.901
I'm honored to have a small role

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:38.534
in Dolly Parton's "Mountain
Magic Christmas" special

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:41.400
tomorrow night on NBC.
I'm in it.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:46.968
Well, it was a big role.
It was a big role,

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:48.434
but after
five minutes of filming,

00:00:48.434 --> 00:00:50.200
Dolly was like, "You know what?
Less is more."

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.200
And I thought it was nice.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.901
What a special night
to have Dolly here.

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:55.434
We actually watched
the Rockefeller Center

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:56.734
Christmas tree lighting
together,

00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:58.634
and once it was lit,
I started singing...

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:03.200
[ To "Jolene" ] ♪ The tree,
the tree, the tree, the tree ♪

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.100
And I'll never forget
what Dolly said.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.167
She said, "Stop that, please."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.467
It was just memorable.

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:11.734
That's right, tonight was
the 90th annual

00:01:11.734 --> 00:01:14.567
Christmas tree lighting
here at Rockefeller Center.

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:16.367
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:19.534
90th.

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:22.834
The crowd -- The crowd
spent hours

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:24.834
waiting in the freezing cold,
the pouring rain,

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:26.801
and 40-mile-per-hour winds.

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:28.934
But at the end of the day,
at least they had

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.934
a beautiful view of
the umbrella in front of them.

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:33.200
I thought that was...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.067
If you couldn't see the lighting
in person, good news,

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:38.934
the tree will be lit daily
from 6:00 a.m. to midnight,

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:41.767
just like everyone
who invested in crypto.

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:44.133
So, there.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:46.000
That's right.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.601
So, the tree is wrapped
in 50,000 lights

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:51.434
and crowned with a star
that has 3 million crystals.

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:52.801
[ Audience oohs ]

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:54.734
Meanwhile, all the other trees
in the city are, like,

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:57.100
"[Coughs] Desperate."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.133
"[Coughs] Sad."

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:01.234
Yep, during tonight's
tree-lighting ceremony,

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:03.634
50,000 lights
were turned on at once.

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:05.467
So, on behalf of everyone here
at 30 Rock,

00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:06.834
I just want to say sorry

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:08.901
to the guy who lives next door
at 32 Rock.

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:10.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:12.567
Let's see what happened
when they lit the tree.

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:15.434
Do we have a video of that guy?

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:18.834
-Time to dust off my collection
of priceless vintage glassware,

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:22.067
which I hope
nothing ever happens to.

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:24.234
Aaah! My eyes!

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:26.200
Aah!
-Oh, my God.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.334
-My glassware!
Aah, my eyes again!

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.067
-Oh, he can't see.
-I'll get you for this,

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:31.868
Rockefeller Center
Christmas tree!

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.567
-I hope he's alright.
I hope he's okay.

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:35.767
-Oh, my gosh!
-I hope he's alright.

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:37.167
-Lucky he had a camera in there.
-Thank goodness

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:39.834
we had the video cameras there
to catch his reaction.

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:41.801
-Both his elbows went up.
-Yeah, I know.

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:43.334
But he knocked both shelves
there.

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:45.467
He didn't know what to do.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.434
-Such a blinding light.
-Yeah, I know.

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:50.968
Meanwhile, though, tonight
in Washington, D.C.,

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:52.701
people were celebrating
the 100th

00:02:52.701 --> 00:02:55.601
national Christmas-tree lighting
with President Biden.

00:02:55.601 --> 00:02:58.968
That's right. We had a tree --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.968 --> 00:03:03.000
a tree lighting in New York
and a tree lighting in D.C.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.767
And then one guy in Philadelphia
microwaved a cheesesteak,

00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:07.067
and the whole East Coast
went dark.

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:09.467
It's like, "Wait, wait."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:11.767
I read that the tree in D.C. is

00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:15.801
about 55 feet shorter than
the one here in New York City.

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:17.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.968 --> 00:03:20.033
The national tree heard and
said, "Hey, it's colder here."

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:22.334
[ Laughter ]
But...

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:24.200
Well, everyone is still talking
about this.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:28.200
The U.S. Men's Soccer Team's big
win over Iran in the World Cup.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.367
Whoa!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:34.567
That's exciting.

00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:37.200
I don't know if anyone's
more excited than Biden.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.200
This is real.
When he found out the result,

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.534
he ran back onstage
after making a speech

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:44.033
to make the announcement,
but his mic wasn't on.

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:45.968
[ Laughter ]
I know.

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:47.334
Watch this. Watch this.

00:03:47.334 --> 00:03:50.334
[ Marching-band music plays ]

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:56.501
♪♪

00:03:56.501 --> 00:03:59.534
[ Laughter ]
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:03.868
-Biden didn't care.

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:05.501
He was finally
living his boyhood dream --

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:06.934
silent film star.
-Aww.

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:08.934
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:10.667
[ Film projector whirring ]

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:13.767
[ Imitating film rewinding ]

00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:17.968
♪♪

00:04:17.968 --> 00:04:19.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:21.634
Some big news --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:21.634 --> 00:04:24.467
You can understand the movie.

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.000
Hey, here's some big news, here.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.434
The Senate just passed
legislation to mandate

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:31.100
federal recognition
for same-sex marriages.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:34.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:41.934
Man, if you thought Iran hated
America after the World Cup,

00:04:41.934 --> 00:04:44.200
oh, boy.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.467
Yep, it's a big deal.
Right after it passed,

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:48.901
Biden awkwardly ran back onstage
to announce it, like...

00:04:48.901 --> 00:04:52.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:55.133
Switching gears,

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:57.000
today Prince William
and Kate Middleton

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.734
arrived in Boston
for their first trip to the U.S.

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:01.767
in nearly 10 years.
-Hmm.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:04.367
-Right?
[ Applause ]

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:06.534
And this was nice.
This was nice.

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:09.200
They met with Boston royalty,
Matt Damon and Ben Affleck.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:13.067
I think Boston is rubbing off
on Prince William.

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:14.834
Just listen to this video
from earlier today.

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:16.234
-[ Boston accent ] Bro,

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:18.067
did you see the Yanks
tank it this year?

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:20.234
I think Judge is coming over
to the Sox.

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:21.767
-Yeah, that's interesting.
-Wow.

00:05:21.767 --> 00:05:23.734
-What's he talking about?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:23.734 --> 00:05:26.167
Get some Dunkin'.

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:28.167
-Well, everyone is talking
about this today.

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:30.901
Spotify released their
annual "Spotify Wrapped."

00:05:30.901 --> 00:05:32.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
Do you all get it?

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:35.534
Yeah.
"Spotify Wrapped" is great.

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:37.033
It reminds me that I've
pretty much been listening

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:39.167
to the same five artists
for the last five years.

00:05:39.167 --> 00:05:41.267
[ Laughter ]
Did you guys see this?

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:42.901
Following a massive
spike in sales,

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:44.701
"The Phantom of the Opera"
has extended

00:05:44.701 --> 00:05:47.334
its final Broadway run
by eight weeks.

00:05:47.334 --> 00:05:51.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:51.367 --> 00:05:53.734
The Phantom was like,

00:05:53.734 --> 00:05:55.968
"I was this close to
not having to wear a mask.

00:05:55.968 --> 00:05:58.200
This -- I mean, almost."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.901
Yeah, they announced
they were closing,

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:01.167
then got record sales.

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:03.734
Now Sears is like,
"We are also closing."

00:06:03.734 --> 00:06:06.133
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.534 --> 00:06:11.434
Well, this is fun.
I saw that next month,

00:06:11.434 --> 00:06:13.534
the world's largest
go-kart track

00:06:13.534 --> 00:06:15.367
is opening in New Jersey.

00:06:15.367 --> 00:06:17.367
[ Audience oohs ]
What took so long?

00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:19.534
It's already the tracksuit
capital of the world.

00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:21.534
I mean, come on.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.534 --> 00:06:23.467
It makes sense, though.
New Jersey is the one place

00:06:23.467 --> 00:06:26.033
you're actually gonna find
a man named Mario in a go-kart.

00:06:26.033 --> 00:06:28.067
So...
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:28.067 --> 00:06:30.167
Come on, that's...

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:33.067
"It's me...Mario."

00:06:33.067 --> 00:06:36.300
And finally, guys,
it's Wednesday.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:37.534
You know what that means?
It's time for

00:06:37.534 --> 00:06:39.400
some "Monday Motivations."

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.701
[ Soft music plays ]
-"Monday Motivations."

00:06:42.701 --> 00:06:45.901
♪♪

00:06:45.901 --> 00:06:47.767
-Secretly, the Kardashians

00:06:47.767 --> 00:06:49.801
are just trying
to keep up with you.

00:06:49.801 --> 00:06:51.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:51.834 --> 00:06:54.000
♪♪

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.601
Every time
you have an appointment,

00:06:55.601 --> 00:06:57.234
your dentist
calls his friends like,

00:06:57.234 --> 00:06:59.601
"You'll never guess
where my hand is right now.

00:06:59.601 --> 00:07:01.801
Yes, Jeffrey's mouth."

00:07:01.801 --> 00:07:04.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:04.767 --> 00:07:08.601
When people see you in a club,
they're like, "Whoa,

00:07:08.601 --> 00:07:10.868
how'd I get into
the VIP section?"

00:07:10.868 --> 00:07:13.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:13.601 --> 00:07:15.300
♪♪

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:17.033
You wore a winter coat
last week,

00:07:17.033 --> 00:07:18.734
and now everyone's wearing
a winter coat.

00:07:18.734 --> 00:07:22.133
That can't be a coincidence.
Congratulations, trendsetter.

00:07:22.133 --> 00:07:25.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:25.167 --> 00:07:27.467
♪♪

00:07:27.467 --> 00:07:30.467
Every time people see you,
they're like, "Mistletoe?"

00:07:30.467 --> 00:07:32.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:32.801 --> 00:07:35.067
♪♪

00:07:35.067 --> 00:07:37.868
When you go down the line and
say what you want at Chipotle,

00:07:37.868 --> 00:07:41.133
the workers are like,
"Right answer, right answer."

00:07:41.133 --> 00:07:45.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:45.033 --> 00:07:47.200
And finally, you're the "you"

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.534
Mariah keeps saying
that she wants for Christmas.

00:07:49.534 --> 00:07:53.367
That's why they play it
every time you go into the CVS!

00:07:53.367 --> 00:07:56.467
All she wants is you!
[ Cheers and applause ]

